1
00:04:43,333 --> 00:04:49,333
He's making a list... pray you're not on it.

2
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:32,666
Santa's Slay is a comedy, fantasy, horror film directed by David Steiman.

3
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Santa Claus is actually a demon who lost a bet with an angel,
so he became the giver of toys and happiness.

4
00:18:53,333 --> 00:18:59,333
But this year the bet is off, and Santa is about to return to his evil ways.

5
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:42,666
Santa, played by Bill Goldberg.

6
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Nicolas Yuleson, played by Douglas Smith.

7
00:33:03,333 --> 00:33:09,333
Mary 'Mac' Mackenzie, played by Emilie de Ravin.

8
00:37:46,666 --> 00:37:52,666
Grandpa, played by Robert Culp.

9
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Pastor Timmons, played by Dave Thomas.

10
00:47:13,333 --> 00:47:19,333
Mr. Green, played by Saul Rubinek.

11
00:51:56,666 --> 00:52:02,666
Santa's Slay is a 2005 Canadian American Christmas black comedy slasher film written and directed
by David Steiman, a former assistant to Brett Ratner; Ratner served as a producer.

12
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
After a millennium of spreading Christmas joy due to losing a bet with an angel, Santa
Claus reverts to his demonic self and gives the gift of evil and fear.

13
01:01:23,333 --> 01:01:29,333
The film stars Bill Goldberg, Douglas Smith, Emilie de Ravin, Robert Culp, Saul
Rubinek, Dave Thomas, Rebecca Gayheart, Chris Kattan, and Fran Drescher.

14
01:06:06,666 --> 01:06:12,666
Santa's Slay was released in the United States on
December 20, 2005, by Media 8 Entertainment.

15
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics.

16
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
The film explores themes of bet, grandparent grandchild
relationship, angel, holiday, mass murder.

17
01:20:16,666 --> 01:20:22,666
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
